===============================================================================
PURPOSE
===============================================================================

This file grants an ADDITIONAL PERMISSION under section 7 of the GNU Affero
General Public License, version 3.0 only ("AGPL-3.0-only"), for the software
distributed with it. It only grants rights; it never removes any right the
AGPL gives you.

Without this Exception, a plugin that uses BaselithCore as a library and is
made available to users over a network would fall under AGPL section 13, and
its author would have to offer the plugin's source code to those users. This
Exception removes that consequence for plugins, and for plugins only. The
framework itself stays copyleft: modify BaselithCore and you still publish
your modifications.

This Exception is offered to everyone on identical terms. It is not limited to
the copyright holder, to its customers, or to plugins published by it.

===============================================================================
1. DEFINITIONS
===============================================================================

"Framework" means the work licensed under AGPL-3.0-only in this distribution —
principally the `core/` directory and any other file the project's SPDX
metadata designates as AGPL-3.0-only — together with any modified version of
it.

"Plugin" means a separate and independent work that:

  (a) is loaded by the Framework's plugin loader from a plugin directory, or
      is designed to be so loaded; and
  (b) interacts with the Framework by using it as a library — for example by
      importing `core.*` modules and by implementing the interfaces the
      Framework publishes for that purpose; and
  (c) does not modify the Framework's own source files.

"Combined Work" means the Framework together with one or more Plugins, whether
distributed together or made available together over a network.

"You" means each recipient of the Framework.

===============================================================================
2. GRANT OF ADDITIONAL PERMISSION
===============================================================================

You may convey a Combined Work, and make a Combined Work available to users
over a computer network, and license each Plugin under terms of your own
choosing — including terms that do not permit disclosure of the Plugin's
source code — without that Plugin becoming subject to AGPL-3.0-only by reason
of the combination.

Sections 5, 6 and 13 of the AGPL, insofar as they require you to offer
Corresponding Source, apply to the Framework and to your modifications of the
Framework. They do not extend to the Plugins.

===============================================================================
3. CONDITIONS
===============================================================================

This Exception applies only while all of the following hold:

  (a) FRAMEWORK STAYS COPYLEFT. Any copy or modified version of the Framework
      that you convey, or that you make available to users over a network,
      remains licensed under AGPL-3.0-only, and its Corresponding Source —
      including your own modifications to it — is offered as sections 5, 6 and
      13 of the AGPL require.

  (b) A PLUGIN IS NOT A FORK. The Plugin does not modify, patch or replace the
      Framework's source files. Code that changes the Framework is a modified
      version of the Framework and is governed by AGPL-3.0-only, whether it is
      shipped inside a plugin directory or anywhere else. Registering handlers,
      routers, middleware, services or configuration through the extension
      points the Framework publishes for that purpose is use of the Framework,
      not modification of it.

  (c) NOTICE. Each Plugin you convey under this Exception states, in its
      documentation or in its own license notice, that it is built for
      BaselithCore, that BaselithCore is licensed under AGPL-3.0-only, and
      where the Corresponding Source of the Framework version it requires can
      be obtained.

  (d) NO ADDITIONAL RESTRICTIONS ON THE FRAMEWORK. You do not impose on any
      recipient of the Framework a term that restricts the rights the AGPL
      grants them in the Framework.

===============================================================================
4. RELATION TO THE AGPL
===============================================================================

This is an additional permission under AGPL section 7. As that section allows,
a recipient may remove this Exception from any copy of the Framework that they
convey, in which case the plain terms of the AGPL govern their copy. Such a
removal does not affect copies conveyed by anyone else, and does not affect a
Plugin already conveyed under this Exception.

If any part of this Exception is held unenforceable, the Framework remains
available to you under the plain terms of AGPL-3.0-only; see the LICENSE file.
Nothing in this Exception weakens the copyleft that applies to the Framework.

===============================================================================
5. SCOPE AND VERSIONING
===============================================================================

This Exception applies to every version of the Framework distributed
accompanied by this file. The copyright holder may publish later versions of
this Exception; each version applies to the releases that carry it, and a new
version never retroactively withdraws a permission already granted for an
earlier release.

===============================================================================
